# Lab 12 Part A: everything that should NOT be sent to the Docker build
# context or copied into the image. One pattern per line, like .gitignore.
#
# TODO Think about each of these and add the patterns that apply to you:
.env
.git/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.db
target/
build/
.gradle/
tests/
docs/
ci/
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
#   * secrets: your .env file (critical: it must never end up in an image)
#   * Git metadata and editor folders (.git/, .vscode/, .idea/)
#   * Python: virtual environments, __pycache__/, .pytest_cache/, local *.db files
#   * Java: target/ or build/ (unless your Dockerfile copies a jar you built
#     outside Docker), .gradle/
#   * files only needed for development: tests, docs, CI config, the
#     Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml themselves
#
# Check your work: the "transferring context" size shown by `docker build`
# should drop noticeably once this file is filled in.
